    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1194">

                <pb facs="1312" n="1300" xml:id="pg1300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.01/7–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the Chairman of the Council of People’s Commissars of the Soviet Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stalin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-07-27">27 July, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Your telegram regarding the Polish situation has been received.<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d1194-f1"/> The Prime Minister tells me that Mikolajczyk is leaving
                    to call on you. It is unnecessary to say that I greatly hope this whole matter
                    with him can be worked out to the best advantage of our common effort by
                    you.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
